cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use claude-dev-star in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "claude-dev-star"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/claude-dev-star"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/claude-dev-star"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A single-file, dependency-free strategy radar for Claude Code sessions. Existing
  dashboards report how many tokens a session burned; this one reports where the effort
  went and whether it moved the operator forward. It reads local Claude Code transcripts,
  classifies each session into a direction using deterministic keyword rules over the
  session title and first user message, and renders a star chart in which each spike is
  one direction and spike length is that direction's share of output tokens. Directions
  are declared by the operator and carry a forward flag, so the tool reports whether the
  sessions agree with the stated goals rather than deciding what progress is; a forward
  direction below a ten percent share is flagged as starving. Output tokens are deduped
  by message id, because Claude Code repeats the usage block on every record of a message
  and naive summing overcounts. No LLM call is made and nothing leaves the machine, which
  makes the classification free, reproducible and auditable by reading a dictionary. Two
  artifacts are written: an HTML chart for the human and a JSON aggregate intended to be
  read back by agents before they propose new work.
keywords:
  - claude-code
  - session-analytics
  - effort-allocation
  - transcript-analysis
  - developer-tools
  - local-first
